A||||3||Rodney||88 rear springs into an 84-87??||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||08-01-2001||10:14 AM||||Since the rear struts interchange for all year Fieros<BR>has anyone ever looked at using the 88 rear coil<BR>springs in an 84-87 to get a smaller diameter spring so<BR>you can put larger rear tires on the rear?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TONY_C||08-01-2001||12:52 PM||||The struts from an '88 do not interchange with the '84-'87 models.  The 3 bolt pattern on the top of the '88 strut is a smaller diameter than what is used on the earlier years. <p>[This message has been edited by TONY_C (edited 08-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||08-01-2001||01:11 PM||||the koni struts are the same part number for all fieros.  however the top mounting plate must be different for 88's.  ive wondered the same thing myself.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||08-01-2001||01:56 PM||||See "Need Help with rear struts"  lower on this list.  KYB doesn't list struts for '88 rear (but they can be mounted, anyway with modification of auto). ||||reg||1
